        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels; Lock, Stock...\n- People: Guy Ritchie; Matthew Vaughn; Jason Flemyng; Dexter Fletcher; Nick Moran; Jason Statham; Steven Mackintosh; Vinnie Jones; Sting\n- Roles: actor; professional footballer; midfielder\n- Organizations: Wimbledon; Leeds United; Sheffield United; Chelsea; Wales\n\nFacts:\n- Vinnie Jones played as a midfielder in professional football from 1984 to 1999 for Wimbledon, Leeds United, Sheffield United, Chelsea, and Wales.\n- Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels is a 1998 British crime comedy film written and directed by Guy Ritchie and produced by Matthew Vaughn.\n- Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels stars Jason Flemyng, Dexter Fletcher, Nick Moran, Jason Statham, Steven Mackintosh, Vinnie Jones, and Sting.\n- Vinnie Jones, born on 5 January 1965, is a British actor and former professional footballer.\n- Lock, Stock... is a 2000 television series spin-off of the 1998 film Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels.",
